B.QR=new A.bO(B.RN,[458907,458873,458978,458982,458833,458832,458831,458834,458881,458879,458880,458805,458801,458794,458799,458800,786544,786543,786980,786986,786981,786979,786983,786977,786982,458809,458806,458853,458976,458980,458890,458876,458875,458828,458791,458782,458783,458784,458785,458786,458787,458788,458789,458790,65717,786616,458829,458792,458798,458793,458793,458810,458819,458820,458821,458856,458857,458858,458859,458860,458861,458862,458811,458863,458864,458865,458866,458867,458812,458813,458814,458815,458816,458817,458818,458878,18,19,392961,392970,392971,392972,392973,392974,392975,392976,392962,392963,392964,392965,392966,392967,392968,392969,392977,392978,392979,392980,392981,392982,392983,392984,392985,392986,392987,392988,392989,392990,392991,458869,458826,16,458825,458852,458887,458889,458888,458756,458757,458758,458759,458760,458761,458762,458763,458764,458765,458766,458767,458768,458769,458770,458771,458772,458773,458774,458775,458776,458777,458778,458779,458780,458781,787101,458896,458897,458898,458899,458900,786836,786834,786891,786847,786826,786865,787083,787081,787084,786611,786609,786608,786637,786610,786612,786819,786615,786613,786614,458979,458983,24,458797,458891,458835,458850,458841,458842,458843,458844,458845,458846,458847,458848,458849,458839,458939,458968,458969,458885,458851,458836,458840,458855,458963,458962,458961,458960,458964,458837,458934,458935,458838,458868,458830,458827,458877,458824,458807,458854,458822,23,458915,458804,21,458823,458871,786850,458803,458977,458981,787103,458808,65666,458796,17,20,458795,22,458874,65667,786994],t.eL)
B.RR={new_word:0,single_choice:1,audio_construct_sentence:2,audio_slide:3,speak_slide:4,gap_typing:5,gap_cards:6,match_cards:7,info_slide:8,voc_spell:9,type_what_you_hear:10,translate_slide:11,video_slide:12,voc_selection:13,dialog_slide:14}
B.QS=new A.bO(B.RR,['This slide type is one of the most important ones in Lezugo. When you create a new_word in a Learn Unit, a new vocabulary item is created in the system. The user can later practice this vocabulary item in the vocabulary trainer, for example in Classic Review or Flashcard Review.\n\nThe vocabulary item can also be used in other slide types, such as voc_selection and voc_spell.\n\nFor a new vocabulary item, you need:\n\u2022 the Armenian text\n\u2022 the Latin transliteration\n\u2022 the English translation\n\u2022 a square example image\n\u2022 an audio recording of the vocabulary item\n\u2022 optionally, an example sentence with the new word, including the Armenian sentence, the English translation, and an audio recording of the Armenian sentence\n\nAlways check whether the vocabulary item already exists in an earlier unit. Use the "Check duplicate" button for this. We want to avoid duplicate vocabulary items in the user\'s vocabulary trainer.\n\nIf you want to introduce a word that should not officially be learned as a vocabulary item, use an audio_slide instead. It offers similar options.\n\nIf an English word has several equivalent Armenian translations, separate them with commas. For example, for "fat", you could enter \u0563\u0565\u0580 and \u0579\u0561\u0572. The user will later be able to enter either accepted variant.\n\nPlease make the English translations as precise as possible to avoid misunderstandings. For example, write bank (financial institution) or bench (for sitting).',"This slide type is a classic quiz. It consists of a question and several answer options.\n\nYou can optionally add an image or audio above the question. This allows the question to refer directly to the image or audio.\n\nIf possible, add a short explanation. It will be shown when the answer is revealed.","The user listens to an Armenian sentence and has to rebuild it using word cards. This exercise is very helpful for improving listening and reading comprehension.\n\nYou need an audio recording for this slide. Enter the text of the recording word by word, in the correct order, as cards.\n\nYou can also add distractors to make the task more difficult. Distractors are word cards containing words that are not heard in the audio. This higher difficulty level should only be used from the middle or end of the beginner level.","This slide type is primarily designed for listening comprehension. In addition to the audio, you can optionally upload an image, enter the audio transcript, add a translation, or include further explanatory text.\n\nThe slide can also consist of only an audio file, without an image or text.\n\nAn Audio Slide is especially useful for example sentences, longer listening passages, or words that should be introduced but should not be added as official vocabulary items via new_word.","This slide type is used to practice pronunciation. You need to upload an audio recording of an Armenian word or sentence and enter what is said in the audio. You also provide the English translation.\n\nThis slide type should not be used too often, because there is currently no technical comparison between the user's recording and the reference audio. The exercise is intended for self-assessment only.\n\nThe user can record themselves, listen to their own recording, and compare it with the original.","This slide type shows one or more sentences with gaps. The gaps are created in the same way as in gap_cards, for example by writing [gap 1] in the sentence.\n\nGap_typing is especially useful for improving the user's writing skills. This slide type can also be used very effectively for grammar exercises.\n\nYou can define a custom instruction.","In this slide type, the user sees one or more sentences with gaps. When entering the sentence, mark the gaps using this format: [gap number].\n\nExample:\n\u0541\u0574\u057c\u0561\u0576\u0568 \u0540\u0561\u0575\u0561\u057d\u057f\u0561\u0576\u0578\u0582\u0574 \u0577\u0561\u057f [gap 1] \u0567 [gap 2]\u0589\n\nTo increase the difficulty, you can add distractors, meaning incorrect word cards. To make the task easier, you can add an audio recording of the text. This is especially useful in the first beginner units to also train listening comprehension.\n\nOptionally, you can upload an image to make the task more visually appealing.",'In this slide type, the user has to match pairs. Each pair consists of an A side and a B side. Each side can contain text, audio, or an image.\n\nText can be entered directly. Audio files and images need to be uploaded.\n\nYou must create at least two pairs. A maximum of four pairs is possible.\n\nBy default, the instruction is "Match the cards." You can change this instruction if it makes sense for the task.',"This slide type is especially useful for explaining information or grammar. It mainly consists of a title and body text. Optionally, you can add a table below the text.\n\nMake sure the table does not become too large. If it has several columns, the user may need to scroll horizontally.\n\nYou can also add media: one audio file and/or one image. The media will be displayed between the title and the text.",'In this slide type, the user sees an English word and has to type the Armenian vocabulary item. There are different difficulty levels.\n\nEasy: The letters of the target word are shown as cards. To use this mode, select the "Use letter cards" option when creating the slide.\nMedium: The letters are shown, and distractors are added. Distractors are incorrect letters that do not appear in the word. To use this mode, also activate the "Use distractors" option.\nHard: No help is shown. Both options are turned off.\n\nFor this slide type, you need an existing vocabulary item that was previously created via new_word in a Learn Unit.',"In this slide type, you provide a word or short sentence as audio. The user has to type what they hear into a text field.",'In this slide type, the user is given an English sentence that they have to translate into Armenian.\n\nYou must always provide a Main Solution. You can also add Solution B and Solution C, which will also be accepted as correct.\n\nThere are two difficulty levels:\n\nNormal: The user sees word cards and has to put them in the correct order.\nHard: Enable the "Free Typing" option. In this mode, there are no word cards. This option should only be used from the middle or end of the beginner lessons and only for shorter sentences.\n\nBelow the default instruction "Translate into Armenian", you can enter a Special Instruction, for example "Use the genitive case".',"For this slide type, you need a title and a YouTube video.\n\nWe may only link to YouTube videos from our own Lezugo channel.\n\nYou can also add a description text that the user can expand below the video.","For this slide type, you select an existing vocabulary item. The vocabulary item must already have been created via new_word in a Learn Unit.\n\nYou then choose one of four learning modes:\n\u2022 En \u2013 Arm: The English translation is shown together with the vocabulary image. The user has to tap the correct Armenian vocabulary item.\n\u2022 Arm \u2013 En: The Armenian vocabulary item is shown. The user has to tap the correct English translation.\n\u2022 Arm \u2013 Image: The Armenian vocabulary item is shown. The user has to select the matching image.\n\u2022 Audio \u2013 En: The user hears the Armenian vocabulary item and has to tap the matching English translation.\n\nRegardless of the mode, the app shows one correct answer and three randomly selected incorrect answers.","For a dialog, you can create up to four conversation participants. Each participant needs a name and a profile image.\n\nWe try to reuse certain characters throughout the app. For these characters, we create a Google Drive folder with fixed profile images and voices that you can reuse.\n\nPlease note: Each part of the conversation must be created separately, with its own audio, text, and translation."],t.l)
